It is an INDEPENDENT reproduction attempt and is not affiliated with the authors of the reproduced
paper. The method is re-implemented from the paper text:

  Huiwen Wu, Xiaogang Xu, Deyi Zhang, Xiaohan Li, Jiafei Wu, Zhe Liu.
  "CG-FedLLM: How to Compress Gradients in Federated Fine-Tuning for Large Language Models."
  ECAI 2025, Frontiers in Artificial Intelligence and Applications vol. 413, pp. 4257-4264,
  IOS Press, doi:10.3233/FAIA251320 (CC BY-NC 4.0); extended version arXiv:2405.13746
  (arXiv license CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). No text or figures of the paper are redistributed.

Behaviour reconstructed (not copied) from third-party software:

  FedIT / FederatedGPT-Shepherd (https://github.com/JayZhang42/FederatedGPT-Shepherd,
  commit bcffa00e9642990ecc6210363a7f0dab91bef4dc), Apache License 2.0. Client sampling, FedAvg
  weighting and the Dolly client partition are independent re-implementations of its semantics.

Runtime dependencies (installed separately, not vendored) include PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause),
Hugging Face transformers / peft / accelerate / datasets / safetensors / huggingface_hub
(Apache-2.0), bitsandbytes (MIT), lm-evaluation-harness (MIT), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause),
PyArrow (Apache-2.0) and PyYAML (MIT).

Model weights and datasets are never stored in this repository. They are downloaded at run time
under their own licenses (see docs/provenance.md).
